  "verbalization": "Dianversicoside G is shown to have a target relationship with Hepatocyte, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including terbutaline and Propenyl propyl disulfide. These compounds are all linked to MOVP-3, suggesting a shared mechanism of action or a common pathway in the cellular response to these molecules. The evidence points to a potential role of Hepatocyte in mediating the effects of Dianversicoside G, with MOVP-3 acting as a downstream target in this process. The integration of these pathways implies that Dianversicoside G may influence cellular processes through Hepatocyte, potentially modulating MOVP-3 activity. The presence of multiple targets in the Hepatocyte pathway supports a broader functional role of this cell type in the context of Dianversicoside G's action.",
